---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Sport & Fitness — 2026/27 Ski + Triathlon Season" description="A dual-season endurance plan: La Diagonela & Vasaloppet on snow, then Ironman 70.3 Rapperswil and the full distance in Port Macquarie — built around a return from injury.">
  <div class="sf">
    <header>
      <div>
        <a href="/ludwig" class="back-link">&larr; Ludwig</a>
        <p class="eyebrow">2026/27 season · Ski + Triathlon · Return from injury</p>
        <h1>Sport &amp; Fitness</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="header-right">
        <strong>17 Oct 2027</strong>
        Ironman Port Macquarie · Australia<br>
        Season A-race · 226 km<br>
        Plan: 3 Aug 2026 – 63 weeks · 5 races
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <!-- Stats -->
      <section>
        <p class="section-label">Season at a glance</p>
        <div class="stat-row">
          <div class="stat-cell"><div class="stat-value">63</div><div class="stat-label">Weeks of preparation</div></div>
          <div class="stat-cell"><div class="stat-value">5</div><div class="stat-label">Race events</div></div>
          <div class="stat-cell"><div class="stat-value">510</div><div class="stat-label">Race kilometres total</div></div>
          <div class="stat-cell"><div class="stat-value">2</div><div class="stat-label">Peaks · winter ski + tri</div></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Race Calendar -->
      <section>
        <p class="section-label">Race calendar</p>
        <div class="race-calendar">
          <div class="race-card r-sprint">
            <div class="race-num">Race 01 · tri</div>
            <div class="race-name">Sprint Triathlon</div>
            <div class="race-date">23 Aug 2026</div>
            <div class="race-meta">25.75 km · 0.75 / 20 / 5</div>
            <span class="race-badge badge-open">First race back</span>
          </div>

          <div class="race-card r-diag">
            <div class="race-num">Race 02 · ski</div>
            <div class="race-name">La Diagonela</div>
            <div class="race-date">17 Jan 2027</div>
            <div class="race-meta">55 km · 1 800 m altitude</div>
            <span class="race-badge badge-ski">Controlled effort</span>
          </div>

          <div class="race-card r-vasa">
            <div class="race-num">Race 03 · ski</div>
            <div class="race-name">Vasaloppet</div>
            <div class="race-date">7 Mar 2027</div>
            <div class="race-meta">90 km · 800 m elevation</div>
            <span class="race-badge badge-winter">Winter peak</span>
          </div>

          <div class="race-card r-703">
            <div class="race-num">Race 04 · tri</div>
            <div class="race-name">Ironman 70.3 Rapperswil</div>
            <div class="race-date">6 Jun 2027</div>
            <div class="race-meta">113 km · 1.9 / 90 / 21.1</div>
            <span class="race-badge badge-tri">Fitness test</span>
          </div>

          <div class="race-card r-full">
            <div class="race-num">Race 05 · tri — main goal</div>
            <div class="race-name">Ironman Port Macquarie</div>
            <div class="race-date">17 Oct 2027</div>
            <div class="race-meta">226 km · 3.8 / 180 / 42.2</div>
            <span class="race-badge badge-target">Target race</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="race-note">
          <strong>One year, two seasons.</strong> It opens with a no-pressure <strong>sprint triathlon (Aug 23)</strong> — a first race back to blow off the cobwebs and test the return, nothing more. The winter races stay on: <strong>La Diagonela (Jan 17)</strong> is a controlled tune-up, <strong>Vasaloppet (Mar 7)</strong> the winter peak. XC skiing is low-impact aerobic gold — it builds the engine that carries into the Ironman while sparing the legs a return-from-injury needs. <strong>Marcialonga is skipped</strong> this year to protect a clean transition. After Vasaloppet you convert to triathlon: <strong>Rapperswil 70.3 (Jun 6)</strong> is a fitness test and race-day rehearsal, and <strong>Port Macquarie (Oct 17)</strong> is the season's only A-race. It is 10+ time zones away, so the taper doubles as a travel plan — arrive early, rehearse the heat, race fresh.
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Season Overview — unified timeline + volume -->
      <section>
        <p class="section-label">Season overview — click a phase to expand</p>
        <div class="season-vis" id="seasonVis">
          <div class="phase-row">
            <div class="phase-bar rehab active" data-phase="rehab" data-start="2026-08-03" data-end="2026-10-11" style="flex:10">
              <span class="phase-bar-name">Rehab &amp; Rebuild</span>
              <span class="phase-bar-sub">10 wks</span>
            </div>
            <div class="phase-bar skibase" data-phase="skibase" data-start="2026-10-12" data-end="2026-12-27" style="flex:11">
              <span class="phase-bar-name">Ski Base</span>
              <span class="phase-bar-sub">11 wks</span>
            </div>
            <div class="phase-bar winter" data-phase="winter" data-start="2026-12-28" data-end="2027-03-07" style="flex:10">
              <span class="phase-bar-name">Winter Races</span>
              <span class="phase-bar-sub">10 wks</span>
            </div>
            <div class="phase-bar tri703" data-phase="tri703" data-start="2027-03-08" data-end="2027-06-06" style="flex:13">
              <span class="phase-bar-name">70.3 Build</span>
              <span class="phase-bar-sub">13 wks</span>
            </div>
            <div class="phase-bar imspec" data-phase="imspec" data-start="2027-06-07" data-end="2027-09-26" style="flex:16">
              <span class="phase-bar-name">IM Specific</span>
              <span class="phase-bar-sub">16 wks</span>
            </div>
            <div class="phase-bar taper" data-phase="taper" data-start="2027-09-27" data-end="2027-10-17" style="flex:3">
              <span class="phase-bar-name">Taper</span>
              <span class="phase-bar-sub">3 wks</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="vol-bars" id="volBars"></div>
          <div class="season-axis">
            <span>Aug</span><span>Oct</span><span>Dec</span><span>Feb</span><span>Apr</span><span>Jun</span><span>Aug</span><span>Oct</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Today needle (spans full vis) -->
          <div class="today-needle" id="todayNeedle">
            <div class="today-line"></div>
            <div class="today-label" id="todayLabel"></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="phase-detail visible" id="detail-rehab">
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Intensity split</div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z1</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z1f" style="width:90%"></div></div><span class="zpct">90%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z2</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z2f" style="width:8%"></div></div><span class="zpct">8%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z3</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z3f" style="width:2%"></div></div><span class="zpct">2%</span></div>
            <div style="margin-top:1.2rem"><div class="dl">Primary disciplines</div>
              <div class="pills"><span class="pill p">Swim</span><span class="pill p">Bike</span><span class="pill p">Roller ski</span><span class="pill">Walk-run</span><span class="pill">Strength</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Weekly volume</div>
            <div class="bignum" style="color:var(--sf-phase-rehab)">5–8</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--sf-ink-3);margin-bottom:1.2rem">hours / week</div>
            <div class="dl">Run reintroduction</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--sf-ink-2);line-height:1.7">Walk-run only, pain-free is the gate<br>Increase run minutes ≤ 10% / wk<br>Load through swim, bike &amp; roller ski</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Key focus points</div>
            <ul class="kp">
              <li>Fix the cause of the injury — rehab work daily, not only when it hurts</li>
              <li>Rebuild the aerobic engine with low-impact swim, bike &amp; roller ski</li>
              <li>Reintroduce running as structured walk-run, strictly pain-free</li>
              <li>Aug 23 sprint tri is a low-key opener — race what you have, keep the run controlled</li>
              <li>Seed winter skills early — easy roller ski &amp; double-pole patterns</li>
              <li>2× strength + mobility per week — hips, posterior chain, single-leg</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Typical week</div>
            <table class="week-table">
              <tr class="rest-row"><td class="wd">Mon</td><td><div class="ws">Rest / mobility</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Tue</td><td><div class="ws">Swim · 45 min</div><div class="wt">Technique + easy aerobic</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Wed</td><td><div class="ws">Bike Z1 · 1 hr</div><div class="wt">Easy spin + strength 30 min</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Thu</td><td><div class="ws">Roller ski Z1 · 1 hr</div><div class="wt">Easy double pole</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Fri</td><td><div class="ws">Walk-run · 30 min</div><div class="wt">Run/walk intervals · pain-free</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sat</td><td><div class="ws">Bike Z1 · 1.5–2 hrs</div><div class="wt">Long easy ride</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sun</td><td><div class="ws">Aqua-jog / mobility</div><div class="wt">Low-impact + strength 2</div></td></tr>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="phase-detail" id="detail-skibase">
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Intensity split</div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z1</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z1f" style="width:80%"></div></div><span class="zpct">80%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z2</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z2f" style="width:15%"></div></div><span class="zpct">15%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z3</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z3f" style="width:5%"></div></div><span class="zpct">5%</span></div>
            <div style="margin-top:1.2rem"><div class="dl">Primary disciplines</div>
              <div class="pills"><span class="pill p">Roller / XC ski</span><span class="pill p">Ski erg</span><span class="pill">Bike</span><span class="pill">Swim</span><span class="pill">Strength</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Weekly volume</div>
            <div class="bignum" style="color:var(--sf-phase-skibase)">8–11</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--sf-ink-3);margin-bottom:1.2rem">hours / week</div>
            <div class="dl">Microcycle</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--sf-ink-2);line-height:1.7">3 build + 1 recovery (~65% vol)<br>On-snow from November onward<br>Run kept minimal — protect the return</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Key focus points</div>
            <ul class="kp">
              <li>Ski-specific aerobic base — this engine carries into the Ironman too</li>
              <li>Double-pole technique &amp; volume grow week over week</li>
              <li>Ski erg bridges the gap until real snow arrives</li>
              <li>Maintain swim &amp; bike lightly; keep running low and pain-free</li>
              <li>Strength for skiing — trunk endurance, lats, posterior chain</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Typical week</div>
            <table class="week-table">
              <tr class="rest-row"><td class="wd">Mon</td><td><div class="ws">Rest</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Tue</td><td><div class="ws">Roller / XC ski Z1 · 2 hr</div><div class="wt">Aerobic double pole</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Wed</td><td><div class="ws">Ski erg + strength · 1.5 hr</div><div class="wt">Trunk + lats</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Thu</td><td><div class="ws">Bike Z1 · 1 hr</div><div class="wt">+ optional short run 20 min</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Fri</td><td><div class="ws">Swim · 45 min</div><div class="wt">Maintain feel</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sat</td><td><div class="ws">Long ski Z1 · 2.5–3 hr</div><div class="wt">Steady aerobic</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sun</td><td><div class="ws">Ski technique · 1.5–2 hr</div><div class="wt">DP refinement</div></td></tr>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="phase-detail" id="detail-winter">
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Intensity split</div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z1</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z1f" style="width:70%"></div></div><span class="zpct">70%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z2</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z2f" style="width:20%"></div></div><span class="zpct">20%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z3</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z3f" style="width:10%"></div></div><span class="zpct">10%</span></div>
            <div style="margin-top:1.2rem"><div class="dl">Primary disciplines</div>
              <div class="pills"><span class="pill p">XC ski</span><span class="pill p">Ski erg</span><span class="pill">Easy bike</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Races this phase</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--sf-ink-2);line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:1.1rem">
              <span style="color:var(--sf-race-a);font-weight:600">La Diagonela · Jan 17</span> — controlled effort<br>
              <span style="color:var(--sf-race-b);font-weight:600">Vasaloppet · Mar 7</span> — winter peak<br>
              <span style="font-size:11px;color:var(--sf-ink-3)">Marcialonga (Jan 31) skipped this year</span>
            </div>
            <div class="dl">Race-pace work</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--sf-ink-2);line-height:1.7">2–3 × 20 min at goal pace weekly<br>Short taper before Vasaloppet</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Key focus points</div>
            <ul class="kp">
              <li>Diagonela is race feel, not a result — 49 days out from Vasaloppet</li>
              <li>Vasaloppet is the winter goal — a clean 2-week taper into it</li>
              <li>Recover cleanly afterward — the whole tri season depends on it</li>
              <li>Double-pole race endurance &amp; pacing confidence</li>
              <li>Wax testing &amp; race logistics dialled before travel</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Typical week</div>
            <table class="week-table">
              <tr class="rest-row"><td class="wd">Mon</td><td><div class="ws">Rest</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Tue</td><td><div class="ws">Race pace · 1.5 hr</div><div class="wt">XC ski · 3×20 min</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Wed</td><td><div class="ws">Easy Z1 · 1 hr</div><div class="wt">Ski erg / walking</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Thu</td><td><div class="ws">Threshold · 1.5 hr</div><div class="wt">XC ski · Z3 efforts</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Fri</td><td><div class="ws">Easy Z1 · 45 min</div><div class="wt">Ski erg</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sat</td><td><div class="ws">Long Z1 · 2–2.5 hr</div><div class="wt">XC ski</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sun</td><td><div class="ws">Easy Z1 · 1 hr</div><div class="wt">XC ski / running</div></td></tr>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="phase-detail" id="detail-tri703">
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Intensity split</div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z1</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z1f" style="width:75%"></div></div><span class="zpct">75%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z2</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z2f" style="width:15%"></div></div><span class="zpct">15%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z3</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z3f" style="width:10%"></div></div><span class="zpct">10%</span></div>
            <div style="margin-top:1.2rem"><div class="dl">Primary disciplines</div>
              <div class="pills"><span class="pill p">Bike</span><span class="pill p">Run</span><span class="pill p">Swim (OWS)</span><span class="pill">Bricks</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Weekly volume</div>
            <div class="bignum" style="color:var(--sf-phase-tri703)">9–11</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--sf-ink-3);margin-bottom:1.2rem">hours / week</div>
            <div class="dl">The transition</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--sf-ink-2);line-height:1.7">Ski left a big aerobic engine — not run legs<br>Rebuild swim feel + run volume from low<br>Careful run ramp given the injury history</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Key focus points</div>
            <ul class="kp">
              <li>One week fully recovered from Vasaloppet before building</li>
              <li>Reintroduce swim &amp; run progressively — bike holds the volume</li>
              <li>Weekly brick: bike → run to train off-the-bike legs</li>
              <li>Open-water swimming as the season warms — sighting, starts</li>
              <li>Rapperswil is a dress rehearsal — pacing &amp; nutrition tested</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Typical week</div>
            <table class="week-table">
              <tr class="rest-row"><td class="wd">Mon</td><td><div class="ws">Rest</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Tue</td><td><div class="ws">Bike threshold · 1.5 hr</div><div class="wt">4×8 min Z3</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Wed</td><td><div class="ws">Swim · 1 hr</div><div class="wt">CSS sets + strength</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Thu</td><td><div class="ws">Run tempo · 45–60 min</div><div class="wt">Building, Z3 blocks</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Fri</td><td><div class="ws">Swim + easy spin</div><div class="wt">Recovery day</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sat</td><td><div class="ws">Long bike · 3 hr</div><div class="wt">With 70.3-pace efforts</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sun</td><td><div class="ws">Brick · bike 1.5 hr + run 30 min</div><div class="wt">Run off the bike</div></td></tr>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="phase-detail" id="detail-imspec">
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Intensity split</div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z1</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z1f" style="width:80%"></div></div><span class="zpct">80%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z2</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z2f" style="width:15%"></div></div><span class="zpct">15%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z3</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z3f" style="width:5%"></div></div><span class="zpct">5%</span></div>
            <div style="margin-top:1.2rem"><div class="dl">Primary disciplines</div>
              <div class="pills"><span class="pill p">Bike (long)</span><span class="pill p">Run (long)</span><span class="pill p">Swim</span><span class="pill">Nutrition</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Weekly volume</div>
            <div class="bignum" style="color:var(--sf-phase-imspec)">12–15</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--sf-ink-3);margin-bottom:1.2rem">hours / week · peak of the year</div>
            <div class="dl">Anchor sessions</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--sf-ink-2);line-height:1.7">Long ride 4.5–6 hr + long run to 2 hr<br>IM effort, not threshold<br>Fuel every long session — no exceptions</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Key focus points</div>
            <ul class="kp">
              <li>Biggest aerobic volume of the year — durability is the goal</li>
              <li>Race-day nutrition &amp; pacing fully dialled in the long sessions</li>
              <li>Ride at IM watts, run at IM effort — rehearse the actual race</li>
              <li>Begin heat preparation for Australia — sauna or overdressed sessions</li>
              <li>Strength drops to maintenance; sleep &amp; recovery become training</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Typical week</div>
            <table class="week-table">
              <tr class="rest-row"><td class="wd">Mon</td><td><div class="ws">Recovery swim / rest</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Tue</td><td><div class="ws">Bike Z2 tempo · 2 hr</div><div class="wt">Sustained aerobic</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Wed</td><td><div class="ws">Swim 1.25 hr + run 45 min</div><div class="wt">Endurance + easy run</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Thu</td><td><div class="ws">Run · 1.25–1.5 hr</div><div class="wt">Z1/Z2 durability</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Fri</td><td><div class="ws">Swim 1 hr + strength</div><div class="wt">Maintenance</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sat</td><td><div class="ws">Long ride · 4.5–6 hr</div><div class="wt">IM watts + nutrition rehearsal</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sun</td><td><div class="ws">Long run · 1.5–2 hr</div><div class="wt">Some off long-ride bricks</div></td></tr>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="phase-detail" id="detail-taper">
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Intensity split</div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z1</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z1f" style="width:80%"></div></div><span class="zpct">80%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z2</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z2f" style="width:15%"></div></div><span class="zpct">15%</span></div>
            <div class="zone-row"><span class="zlbl">Z3</span><div class="ztrack"><div class="zfill z3f" style="width:5%"></div></div><span class="zpct">5%</span></div>
            <div style="margin-top:1.2rem"><div class="dl">Primary disciplines</div>
              <div class="pills"><span class="pill p">Swim</span><span class="pill p">Bike</span><span class="pill p">Run</span><span class="pill">Travel</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Volume cut</div>
            <div class="bignum" style="color:var(--sf-phase-taper)">&minus;45%</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--sf-ink-3);margin-bottom:1.2rem">from peak week</div>
            <div class="dl">TSB target race morning</div>
            <div class="bignum" style="font-size:1.8rem">+5 to +20</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Key focus points</div>
            <ul class="kp">
              <li>Volume down sharply, frequency stays — short race-pace bursts keep sharpness</li>
              <li>Fly to Australia 10–14 days early — beat the 10+ hour time change</li>
              <li>Finish heat acclimation before race week, not during it</li>
              <li>Lock logistics: bike build, nutrition supply, race-morning timeline</li>
              <li>Race: swim controlled, bike to power &amp; nutrition plan, run within yourself</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="dc">
            <div class="dl">Typical week</div>
            <table class="week-table">
              <tr class="rest-row"><td class="wd">Mon</td><td><div class="ws">Rest</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Tue</td><td><div class="ws">Bike · 1.5 hr</div><div class="wt">Short race-pace bursts</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Wed</td><td><div class="ws">Swim 45 min + run 30 min</div><div class="wt">Sharpeners</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Thu</td><td><div class="ws">Bike 1 hr + run 20 min</div><div class="wt">Easy brick / travel</div></td></tr>
              <tr class="rest-row"><td class="wd">Fri</td><td><div class="ws">Easy swim / travel day</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sat</td><td><div class="ws">Shakeout · swim-bike-run</div><div class="wt">Short openers</div></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="wd">Sun</td><td><div class="ws" style="font-weight:700;color:var(--sf-ink)">Race day</div></td></tr>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>



      <!-- Principles -->
      <section>
        <p class="section-label">Core principles</p>
        <div class="principles">
          <div class="principle"><div class="pnum">01</div><div class="ptitle">Aerobic base first</div><div class="pbody">~80% of all time below the first threshold. Z2 is the danger zone — the most common mistake is drifting there on easy days. Easy stays genuinely easy; both a Vasaloppet and an Ironman are won aerobically.</div></div>
          <div class="principle"><div class="pnum">02</div><div class="ptitle">Consistency over heroics</div><div class="pbody">Coming back from injury, the plan only works if you stay healthy. Ramp run volume ≤10%/week, keep rehab work daily, never chase a missed session. Twelve boring weeks beat one brilliant one.</div></div>
          <div class="principle"><div class="pnum">03</div><div class="ptitle">Skiing is low-impact base</div><div class="pbody">The winter block isn't a detour — XC skiing builds a huge aerobic engine while sparing the legs. That base converts directly into the spring triathlon build, and the races keep training fun.</div></div>
          <div class="principle"><div class="pnum">04</div><div class="ptitle">3 + 1 microcycle</div><div class="pbody">Three build weeks, one recovery week (~65% volume). Adaptation happens during recovery — the build only creates the stimulus. Non-negotiable while returning from injury.</div></div>
          <div class="principle"><div class="pnum">05</div><div class="ptitle">Race the calendar in order</div><div class="pbody">Diagonela controlled, Vasaloppet the winter peak, Rapperswil a rehearsal, Port Macquarie the A-race. Each serves the next — never let an earlier race compromise a later one. Marcialonga is dropped to keep the transition clean.</div></div>
          <div class="principle"><div class="pnum">06</div><div class="ptitle">Race the travel</div><div class="pbody">Port Macquarie is 10+ time zones away. The taper is also a travel plan: arrive 10–14 days early, adapt to the reversed day, and rehearse heat &amp; nutrition long before race week.</div></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <span>Sport &amp; Fitness · 2026/27 ski + tri season · v2.1</span>
      <span>3 Aug 2026 – 17 Oct 2027 · 5 races · intervals.icu compatible</span>
    </footer>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

